# Shell scripts must arrive as LF regardless of the checkout's core.autocrlf.
#
# The repo is normally cloned onto a Windows path and the scripts are run from
# WSL (see README "Development"). With core.autocrlf=true — the Windows default —
# a checkout rewrites them to CRLF, and bash then reads the shebang as
# `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, failing with "bad interpreter: ... ^M". Every .sh here
# is already stored LF, so this pins existing behavior rather than changing it.
*.sh text eol=lf
